      Inflatable Pool Factory destructive testing SOP (factory QMS controlled document WI-QC-DS-2026-001, V1.0):
      sampling at first-article inspection and periodic in-production intervals draws three finished units plus one
      fabric offcut roll per sample set, each unit with a dedicated role (material, process, structure) and bound
      traceability records (fabric supplier and roll, coating and edge-tape lots, adhesive lots, welding machine ID,
      operator badge). Stage 1 material tests: coating 180° peel (mean ≥120 N/5 cm, valley ≥100 N/5 cm, cohesive fiber
      failure required), pressurized single-point puncture at rated working pressure Pw (peak ≥350 N, tear propagation
      ≤30 mm with a 1.0 mm hemispherical pin), and a -18°C 180° cross-fold under a 5 kg weight with a 3-minute 10 PSI
      soap-water leak check (no crazing, no bubbles). Stage 2 process tests: 55°C / 1.5× Pw 48-hour creep on a full unit
      (wall-thickness expansion ≤10%, witness-line shift ≤1.0 mm, pressure drop ≤8%, zero seam leaks) followed by a
      step-up burst test at +2.0 PSI stages inside an explosion-proof cage (ultimate burst pressure ≥2.5× Pw, ≥3.0× Pw
      for premium models, first failure point located on high-speed video). Stage 3 structural tests: 100% overload
      water fill held 72 hours (outward tilt ≤10°, no interior floor-to-wall seam whitening or delamination), a 150 kg
      60-minute rim load with no fold buckling, 500 pendulum impacts from a 1.0 m release with a post-impact 1.5× Pw
      60-minute soap check, destructive valve torque ≥25 N·m and drain pull-out ≥800 N. Failures are routed by a
      diagnostic matrix to material (IQC), process (IPQC) or design (R&D) ownership with corrective and preventive
      actions (CAPA) issued within 48 hours; the raw-data record sheet carries per-test measured values, per-item
      PASS/FAIL and the lot disposition. Routine non-destructive QC on every unit is described on the quality-control
